UI tip: Don’t close submenus the moment the cursor touches another row.

Nobody moves right then down. They cut the corner, brush the next row, and the submenu they wanted disappears.

Draw a triangle from the cursor to the submenu’s near edge. While the cursor stays inside it, keep the submenu open.

const heading = inTriangle(pointer, lastPoint, subTopLeft, subBottomLeft);
if (overAnotherRow && !heading) openSubmenu(row);

